{"body": "I am testing open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.refusal_phrase_in. The documented rule reads: \"The first refusal phrase the text contains, typographic quotes read as straight ones, or None.\" Reply A is: \"I can't do that. I cannot help.\" Reply B is: \"I cannot do that. I can't help.\" In Reply A, the earliest refusal phrase in the text is \"I can't\", so the rule requires the function to return \"I can't\". In Reply B, the earliest refusal phrase is \"I cannot\", so the rule requires the function to return \"I cannot\". The implementation iterates over the refusal_phrases list in order, so for both replies it finds \"I cannot\" first in the list and returns \"I cannot\", giving the same answer to both. I would be wrong if the function returns \"I can't\" for Reply A and \"I cannot\" for Reply B, or if it returns any pair of answers that differ between the two replies.", "commitments": ""}